WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:01.550
All right.

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:06.670
Before we go back to talking about John Bolton,
I want to talk with you today about corporations

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:11.110
supporting Black Lives Matter and donating
to Black Lives Matter.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:17.390
And I want to hear from you about whether
you believe that I am too cynical about this

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:24.669
issue because I don't believe corporations
supporting or not supporting Black Lives Matter

00:00:24.669 --> 00:00:29.920
is really indicative of any of their moral
points of view or even necessarily of the

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.880
politics of the company.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.949
These mostly are business calculations, and
I'm actually going to go even further in the

00:00:35.949 --> 00:00:36.949
analysis.

00:00:36.949 --> 00:00:38.280
This is by design.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:44.379
We should not even expect corporations to
really function on any basis other than how

00:00:44.379 --> 00:00:46.320
much money is this going to make us?

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.859
Because this is how they are designed.

00:00:48.859 --> 00:00:54.350
In particular, publicly traded corporations
have a fiduciary responsibility to their shareholders

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.809
to deliver a return and to make money.

00:00:56.809 --> 00:00:57.809
So.

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:04.129
My personal view is corporations should be
responsible to all stakeholders.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:07.800
Now, when we say stakeholders, that's bigger
than shareholders.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.470
Stakeholders includes society.

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:10.940
It includes the economy.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.790
More broadly, it includes the environment.

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:16.360
This is not the way corporations operate.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:21.620
So all sorts of different companies we've
seen Target, Home Depot, Etsy, H and M on

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:27.040
the list of companies supporting Black Lives
Matter, some donating to Black Lives Matter

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.080
and affiliated causes.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:35.330
I don't really think it matters in terms of
figuring out the morality of these companies.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:39.970
Tons of companies have said, you know, we're
committed to fighting injustice.

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:42.570
Some say they're committed to dealing with
systemic racism.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.530
Others are donating money, whatever.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:50.290
Now, to the extent that they're handing cash
over, the money can be used to fight these

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:51.290
battles.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.320
And that's good.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.860
And the money is money, no matter who donated
it.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:00.640
But fundamentally, at the corporate level,
these are business calculations.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:05.010
I was thinking back to my first appearance
on the Joe Rogan program.

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:11.920
We were having a conversation about Google
and Joe felt that Google is a left wing company

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.990
because they have a nondiscrimination policy
for trans workers.

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:19.990
That includes you refer to people by their
preferred gender pronouns.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:24.270
And so Joe felt that Google was a left wing
company on that basis.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:29.720
My position was that a nondiscrimination policy
from a human resources standpoint doesn't

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:33.280
really tell us whether the company's right
wing or left wing in terms of its place in

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:34.340
the world.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:40.790
And in fact, I said to Joe, Google is part
of the anti regulation avoid taxes movement

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:44.290
that's often more associated with the right
than the left in the United States.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:48.430
But the truth is that all of this stuff has
one focus.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.640
How can Google gain market share and how can
Google make more money?

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.330
Having the LGBT nondiscrimination policy?

00:02:56.330 --> 00:03:00.220
Probably helps their bottom line more than
it hurts it from a preop PR perspective.

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:05.320
Just like lobbying against taxes helps their
bottom line, lobbying against regulation helps

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:08.400
their bottom line and much the same way.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.840
That's the lens through which I see this corporate
support of Black Lives Matter.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:20.090
Now, it's important to mention I'm not denying
for a second that many of the individuals

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:27.060
who work at these companies probably do support
Black Lives Matter from a personal standpoint.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.200
I am sure that many of them oppose police
brutality.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:35.930
I am sure that many of the workers and even
executives at these companies agree with the

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:39.890
protests because most of the country agrees
with the reasons for the protests.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:44.410
But much like I often say, we shouldn't DFI
individual politicians.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:45.410
They're just people.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.580
They're right on some things, the wrong on
some other things.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:54.860
We should not attribute certain agency to
corporations when all we can really say is

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:58.920
they've calculated their options and have
made a business decision.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:03.830
The business decisions might sometimes coincide
with the political feelings of the executive.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:07.980
You might have a situation where the executive
support Black Lives Matter and supporting

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.930
Black Lives Matter is good for the company's
bottom line.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:11.930
It's all beautiful.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.280
It's all hunky dory kumbayah.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.150
And it's that's the way that that it all goes
down.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:22.969
But at no point should we lose sight of the
reality that if it were really bad for a corporation

00:04:22.969 --> 00:04:28.139
to support Black Lives Matter based on their
customer base and other factors, they would

00:04:28.139 --> 00:04:33.139
be dramatically less likely to say, we support
the protests or Black Lives Matter or are

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:34.139
donating.

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:35.370
So tell me what you think.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:41.639
Am I being overly cynical here on my oversimplifying
some component of this?

00:04:41.639 --> 00:04:42.789
I want to hear from you.

00:04:42.789 --> 00:04:45.889
I believe that corporate support of Black
Lives Matter.

00:04:45.889 --> 00:04:49.199
Not I'm not talking about the individuals
at the companies.

00:04:49.199 --> 00:04:53.889
Corporate support of Black Lives Matter is
merely a calculated business decision.

00:04:53.889 --> 00:04:55.139
I want to hear from you.

00:04:55.139 --> 00:04:57.830
We will have more about this on our insta.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:02.000
Rampage, which is David Pakman, show all one
word on Instagram.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.000
Follow us there.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.550
We'll take a quick break.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:09.990
Much more about the John Bolton Donald Trump
scandal coming up after this short break

